    "name": "辅音 + 元音连读",
    "formal": "not at all",
    "sound": "nodadall",
    "tip": "前一个词以辅音结尾、后一个以元音开头时，两个词黏成一个词。"
  },
  {
    "id": "r02",
    "name": "闪音（t / d → 轻 d）",
    "formal": "better water",
    "sound": "bedder wader",
    "tip": "两个元音之间的 t 会变成很轻的 d，这是美音最明显的特征。"
  },
  {
    "id": "r03",
    "name": "h 音脱落",
    "formal": "tell him",
    "sound": "tellim",
    "tip": "him / her / he 在句中常丢掉 h。"
  },
  {
    "id": "r04",
    "name": "to 弱读",
    "formal": "want to go",
    "sound": "wanna go",
    "tip": "to 在句中退化成 /tə/，快到几乎听不见。"
  },
  {
    "id": "r05",
    "name": "of 弱读",
    "formal": "a lot of",
    "sound": "a lotta",
    "tip": "of 退化成 /ə/ 甚至完全吞掉。"
  },
  {
    "id": "r06",
    "name": "for 弱读",
    "formal": "for the team",
    "sound": "fer the team",
    "tip": "for 在句中读 /fər/，不是 /fɔːr/。"
  },
  {
    "id": "r07",
    "name": "and 弱读",
    "formal": "bread and butter",
    "sound": "bread n butter",
    "tip": "and 只剩一个 /ən/ 甚至 /n/。"
  },
  {
    "id": "r08",
    "name": "did you 合流",
    "formal": "did you",
    "sound": "didja",
    "tip": "d + y 合成 /dʒ/。同理 wouldja、couldja。"
  },
  {
    "id": "r09",
    "name": "what are you 合流",
    "formal": "what are you doing",
    "sound": "whaddaya doing",
    "tip": "四个音节压成一个词。"
  },
  {
    "id": "r10",
    "name": "失去爆破",
    "formal": "next day",
    "sound": "nex day",
    "tip": "两个爆破音相遇，前一个只做口型不出声。"
  },
  {
    "id": "r11",
    "name": "have 缩写",
    "formal": "should have",
    "sound": "shoulda",
    "tip": "shoulda / coulda / woulda，母语者几乎不读 have。"
  },
  {
    "id": "r12",
    "name": "give me / let me",
    "formal": "give me",
    "sound": "gimme",
    "tip": "同理 lemme、tell me → \"telly-me\"。"
  },
  {
    "id": "r13",
    "name": "I don't know",
    "formal": "I do not know",
    "sound": "I dunno",
    "tip": "极高频，几乎总是读成 \"I dunno\"。"
  },
  {
    "id": "r14",
    "name": "you 弱读",
    "formal": "keep you posted",
    "sound": "keepya posted",
    "tip": "you 在句中退化成 /jə/，与前词黏连。"
  },
  {
    "id": "r15",
    "name": "句末 t / d 弱化",
    "formal": "I just got it",
